'' A FIELD NAMED BY A KEYWORD, WITH AN INITIALISER: 'Open as boolean = true'. The keyword-named
'' branch of a TYPE body read the name, the bounds, a width and the type, but not the '= value'
'' (or '=> value') the name-first branch reads, so the '=' was TKO0420 "expected the end of the
'' statement" (tkEdit TK-002). MEASURED, fbc-modern 1.20: all thirty statement keywords probed
'' (Open Close Name Line Input Print Get Put Seek Lock Write Read Data Color Width Error Erase
'' Screen Draw Swap Lset Rset Poke Paint Pset Circle Palette Window ...) take an initialiser,
'' and this program prints the line below.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/parser/src/field-keyword-init.bas -o tests/parser/field-keyword-init.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/parser/field-keyword-init.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: true            7            nm             2             3
